<title>USA: Brazos, Texas, finance agency plans taxable notes.</title>
<headline>Brazos, Texas, finance agency plans taxable notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazos Student Finance Corp, Texas, plans to sell as much as $300 million of asset-backed taxable notes in July, chief executive officer Murray Watson said Monday.</p>
<p>The notes, which would be backed by student loans, would be sold via Smith Barney Inc, Watson said. In March, the corporation sold roughly $60 million of tax-exempt bonds, he said.</p>
<p>--Kathie O'Donnell, 212-859-1650</p>
